# Everything the image does not need, and one thing it must not have.
#
# `target/` is the important one: a jar built on a laptop is built against that laptop's JDK
# and whatever was in the working tree at the time, and copying it in would make the image a
# snapshot of somebody's machine rather than of this commit.
target/
.git/
.github/
.idea/
docs/
scripts/
*.md
